            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>Your house scored well in the air tightness test at 1.32 airchanges per hour (ACH). I found few air leak locations- just around the garage door (replace the weather stripping and, or add a second layer) and through ligth switches and electrical outlets on exterior walls. There are foam gaskets that fit behind the face plates that can reduce air leaks.</airSeal>
                <foundation>Your basement is one of the two areas of greatest heat loss in the house so, as we discussed, I added two inches of high density spray foam (R12.6) to the floor of the basement and two inches of rigid foam insulation (R-10) to the basement walls. This reduced the heat lost through the basement by 45% or 14 gigajoules per year.</foundation>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
